# The index keeps LF for every text file, so a checkout on any platform parses
# the same bytes. The DSL is the reason this matters: a stray CR reattributes a
# section to the one above it, and content is authored by pasting through GitHub.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Union keeps both sides of a conflicting hunk. That is exactly right for an
# append-only log — two branches appending events collide on the last line for
# no reason a human can adjudicate, and keeping both is always the answer.
#
# It is wrong for the store, whose records are edited rather than only appended.
# Two branches editing one record would keep both copies under one id; `doctor`
# reports that and exits 0, so CI stays green while every read answers from the
# first copy forever and `edit` writes both back. A conflict is loud and
# fixable. A silent duplicate is neither.
docs/events.jsonl merge=union

# Windows tooling that needs its own line endings whatever the repo says.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
